# Project Structure

## `dev/` Directory

The `dev/` directory contains project-level documentation and tooling that is not shipped to production.

| Directory | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `dev/plans/` | Implementation plans for features and refactors. One Markdown file per plan. |
| `dev/rules/` | Project rules and conventions for Claude and contributors. One `.mdc` file per topic. |
| `dev/test/` | Test utilities, fixtures, and helpers not co-located with source. |

## Rules for Claude

- Always write plans to `dev/plans/`, never to `~/.claude/plans/` or any other private directory.
- Always write project rules to `dev/rules/`.
- Never create files outside the project workspace for project-related content.
